  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Libya Storm Daniel Resilience, Recovery and Reconstruction Plan in Libya (Sept 2023 - Sept 2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 9 September 2023, Storm Daniel made landfall in Libya, causing substantial rainfall and sudden floods in the northeast regions and coastal cities, with Derna municipality being the most affected. This resulted in a high number of casualties and population displacement, including migrant workers living in some of the most flood-affected areas. There are significant needs in the aftermath of the storm, including accommodation, health services and food. 
 
In line with its Resilience, Recovery and Reconstruction Plan, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is contributing to improving the humanitarian situation and supporting the recovery and resilience of flood-affected populations in northeastern Libya. Specifically, through this project, IOM is assisting 28,040 disaster-affected individuals with health, water, sanitation and hygiene, socio-economic recovery and disaster risk reduction.</narrative>
  </description>
